e the station  effectively has infinite inertia it  doesn't move whenever they fire the guns  and with six of them placed around the  surface the station can rain hell on any  point inside the ring space it is the  perfect defense setup and one they  didn't anticipate because they never  realized they could use the station in  that way they discount using a fast nuke  attack to destroy medina because the  last time they detonated nukes near the  station it powered up and nearly  destroyed the entire solar system there  is a chance to intercept the pella  before they get there but the window is  closing fast plus it would require them  to abandon series and let everyone there  die and there's still a pretty fair  chance that they wouldn't be able to win  the military commanders from the un and  mars are both in favor of this plan but  abasarala is hesitant she tells them  that they'll have her decision soon and  dismisses them  bobby stays behind and avasarala  explains that she refused to go along  with the strike on medina and she  wonders if she's gone too soft was she  trying too hard to be good when she  should have been ruthless bobby starts  out trying to be diplomatic but things  escalate to where she says fine maybe  you have gone a bit soft which might not  be so bad in small doses but now is not  the time for self-pity [ __ ] it's  time to keep your eyes on the enemy and  wait for the next time they slip up  because i still think we're the good  guys and i'd rather do a little less  soul searching and a lot more fighting  back abasarallah definitely takes in  what she's saying but tells her to go do  something else and dismisses her like  the others on the rossi we get one more  character return via a cameo by elvi who  is talking to naomi about the missing  ship data this was the person that  holden mentioned that might know more  about what was going on there they  noticed that there is a mass energy  threshold that precedes or perhaps  triggers the disa